      "bullets": [
        "CNBC reported on 15 October that Anthropic's \"third-quarter revenue stands at $16.8 billion\", that \"Revenue rose from $11.6 billion in the second quarter, with first-quarter revenue at $4.7 billion, the people said, adding that Anthropic said it was profitable on an adjusted basis in the third quarter\", and that the company \"was cash-flow positive, generating $1.70 in revenue for every dollar spent on computing power during the third quarter, according to the Financial Times\". CNBC wrote that \"Investors expect Anthropic to reach $110 billion in annualized revenue by year-end, according to The Wall Street Journal,\" and that the IPO is \"reportedly slated for November\".",
        "Business Day, carrying the Reuters account, reported that \"Anthropic's third-quarter revenue rose more than 45% to $16.8bn from the previous quarter, according to an investor who attended a pre-IPO meeting with Anthropic leadership in San Francisco on Wednesday.\" Seoul Economic Daily, compiling foreign reports as of 15 October, put distillation-related revenue at \"5% to 7% of total, significantly cut in Q3\", recorded \"The revenue growth rate fell to 45% from 142%\", gave an adjusted operating margin of 11%, and headlined the week's valuation move as a $500 billion fall. Reuters reported on 16 October that \"the Financial Times reported on Friday\" that Anthropic is offering Blackstone \"a yield of more than 10%\" on \"$9 billion\" of five-year chip lease payments, adding that \"Reuters could not immediately verify the report.\"",
        "On 18 October Anthropic published its own figure: \"Subject to stockholder approval, 5% of Anthropic's shares will be committed today,\" to a wholly owned LLC called the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund, \"with an additional 2% added at the board's discretion for every 50% increase in the company's value above a set baseline\". Anthropic wrote that \"roughly 20% of Anthropic shares will be dedicated to the public good\" and that \"None of the Anthropic equity held by the LLC will be used for lobbying or political giving, in the US or abroad\". CNBC reported the baseline \"has yet to be disclosed\".",
        "The revenue and distillation figures rest on one secondhand account of a closed investor meeting, relayed by the Financial Times, The Information and The Wall Street Journal; no Anthropic filing carries them. Anthropic has confidentially filed for a US IPO but has published no prospectus. Lise Buyer of Class V Group told CNBC the benefit-fund timing is \"both mandatory to prepare for an initial public offering, and 'beneficial from an image perspective'\"."
